{"_comment": "One row per employer, joining what was REQUESTED (DOL labour condition applications, with the promised wage level), what was GRANTED (USCIS approvals and denials) and what was FOUND (Wage and Hour Division violations). NAMES ARE THE WHOLE DIFFICULTY: the three agencies share no identifier and each employer files under several spellings, so names are normalised for case, punctuation and legal suffixes and matched EXACTLY -- nothing is fuzzy-matched, and every company total is therefore a FLOOR. Each row lists the spellings it merged so the join can be audited. THE INPUTS ARE TOP-N EXTRACTS, not full registers: an employer absent from the enforcement list has no findings IN THAT EXTRACT, which is not the same as having none. NO EQUIVALENT EXISTS FOR L-1 OR O-1 -- neither requires a labour condition application and USCIS publishes no employer hub for either, so this question cannot be asked of them at all.", "sources": {"requested": "US DOL OFLC, H-1B LCA disclosure data", "granted": "USCIS H-1B Employer Data Hub, FY2009-2023", "enforcement": "US DOL Wage and Hour Division (WHISARD)"}, "employers": 84, "in_uscis_and_lca": 21, "with_enforcement": 37, "not_published_by_employer": ["L-1", "O-1"], "profiles": [{"canonical": "COGNIZANT TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS", "names": ["COGNIZANT TECH SOLNS US CORP", "COGNIZANT TECH SOLUTIONS US CORP", "COGNIZANT TECHNOLOGY SOLNS US CORP", "COGNIZANT TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS US", "COGNIZANT TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS US CORP"], "initial_approvals": 50940, "continuing_approvals": 139841, "initial_denials": 11465, "lca_filings": 43264, "low_level_filings": 21935, "enforcement_cases": null, "back_wages": null, "employees_covered": null, "spellings": 5, "display": "Cognizant Tech Solns Us Corp", "low_level_pct": 50.7, "initial_denial_rate_pct": 18.4, "absent_from": ["enforcement"], "sources": ["uscis", "lca"]}, {"canonical": "TATA CONSULTANCY SERVICES", "names": ["TATA CONSULTANCY SERVICES LIMITED", "TATA CONSULTANCY SVCS LTD"], "initial_app